                <head>485. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The United States ratified the Convention on the Territorial Sea and the
                    Contiguous Zone (15 UST 1606), the Convention on the High Seas (13 UST 2312),
                    the Convention on Fishing and Conservation of the Living Resources of the High
                    Seas (17 UST 138), and the Convention on the Continental Shelf (15 UST 471) on
                    March 24, 1961. All four conventions had been signed by the United States on
                    September 15, 1958, and had received the advice and consent of the Senate on May
                    26, 1960. The United States deposited its ratifications with the
                    Secretary-General of the United Nations on April 12, 1961.</p>
            </div>
